{"id":"resp_8af00afd1f9f0ab9","created_at":1795618552,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_96626ed48ebc4994","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to output revised SHACL, fixing ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR: target classes beyond declared population. The declaration's focus_set owner_class is ship (https://w0ld...). So target must be ship, not internalIceStrengthenedStructure? Actually shape Ship uses targetClass nltl:ship, ok. The other shapes targetClass qudt:QuantityValue (that's okay, not part of focus set? Probably fine). internalIceStrengthenedStructure shape targetClass nltl:internalIceStrengthenedStructure – this is outside declared population (owner class is ship). The error says \"Other target classes select beyond declared population\". So need to constrain activation to population boundary, not to target other classes. According to suggestion: Constrain activation to supplied population boundary. Preserve everything else. So we must remove or guard the internalIceStrengthenedStructure shape, or make it not targetClass but maybe a property shape applied via path from ship? The requirement is to keep internal structure shape? The instruction: \"Do not delete constraints merely to pass checks ... Remove or replace an excessive constraint only when supplied source/schema supports that change.\" There's evidence that internalIceStrengthenedStructure is linked and has property internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition, but it's not within the declared population; it's part of the model, but the admission only covers ship class. So we should not have a target on internalIceStrengthenedStructure – that's beyond scope. Instead, we can keep the shape but make it a property shape on ship rather than its own NodeShape targeting that class. Could embed its constraints in the Ship shape via path (already done via QuantityValueShape). InternalIceStrengthenedStructure shape is essentially redundant. The instruction: avoid deleting constraints unless supported. We have evidence that modelPaths includes internalIceStrengthenedStructure as an intermediate but target_owner is null - implying ambiguous. Since the focus set is ship, we cannot validate internalIceStrengthenedStructure as separate target. So we should remove that shape entirely, as it's not needed (its constraints are already enforced). Evidence supports that internal structure must have property pointing to QuantityValue, which is already enforced via ship shape. So we can delete the InternalIceStrengthenedStructure shape, as it's not required and outside scope.\n\nAlso \"UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT\" on sh:targetClass line 14 column 20 (that's the QuantityValueShape targetClass qudt:QuantityValue). The message \"Target cannot be bound to an explicit model owner\". The modelPaths in evidence says owners: corrosionAbrasionAllowance: plating, hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure: ship, internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition: internalIceStrengthenedStructure, polarClassRequirementsApplicable: ship. target_owner null. So maybe targetClass qudt:QuantityValue is not part of the model owner's classes? The quantity is a QUDT value used as representation; likely it's okay, but the error suggests we cannot bind targetClass to a class not in model owners. However the context contract likely expects representation only node shapes, not targetClass? The previous shape used sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue, which may be okay, but error indicates cannot be bound to explicit model owner. Perhaps we should use sh:targetObjectsOf the property that uses QuantityValue, rather than targetClass. For the QuantityValue shape, instead of targeting class, we could apply it via sh:node on the path, as done in Ship shape. But we still need a shape to validate QuantityValue nodes, but we can define it as a shape without targetClass, and reference via sh:node. So remove sh:targetClass and rely on node shape usage. That should address unresolved context.\n\nThus revise: QuantityValueShape: remove sh:targetClass, keep properties. Ship shape remains same. Remove InternalIceStrengthenedStructureShape. Ensure all prefixes unchanged.\n\nNow produce <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL>. Ensure candidate_version and sha remain same? The instruction: produce COMPLETE revised SHACL bound to candidate_version and candidate_sha256. Likely same version and sha must match? But we will produce new SHACL; the sha will change, but they said bound to candidate_version and candidate_sha256, meaning we keep those values in metadata? There's no metadata fields; just use same candidate_version in naming? Not needed. Just output SHACL.\n\nLet's construct final SHACL.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_b7ac052b58be610a","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape: QuantityValue – represents the corrosion/abrasion addition\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:QuantityValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    rdfs:comment \"QuantityValue node that must encode the corrosion/abrasion addition as exactly 1.0 mm per I2‑11.3. Units and datatype are fixed by the locked representation context.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:maxInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Numeric value must be exactly 1.0 (decimal), per the source requirement.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:MilliM ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Unit must be the canonical QUDT millimetre unit.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape: Ship – applies the corrosion/abrasion addition requirement\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ShipCorrosionAbrasionAdditionShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    rdfs:comment \"\"\"This shape encodes the requirement from I2‑11.3:\n    “Polar Class ships are to have a minimum corrosion/abrasion addition of ts = 1.0 mm applied to all internal structures within the ice‑strengthened hull areas…”.\n\n    The applicability to Polar‑Class ships is recorded in the source but the exact activation\n    (e.g., presence/true value of nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable) is ambiguous in the supplied data.\n    Consequently, this shape validates the numeric/units constraints for every ship instance; callers may\n    apply additional filtering based on their own eligibility assertions.\n    \"\"\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        # Path: ship → internalIceStrengthenedStructure → corrosion addition quantity value\n        sh:path ( nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition ) ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n        rdfs:comment \"Each internal ice‑strengthened structure linked from a ship must have an associated corrosion/abrasion addition matching the QuantityValueShape.\" ;\n    ] .\n</END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":39580,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":320,"cache_write_tokens":39248,"input_tokens_per_turn":[39580],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[320]},"output_tokens":1526,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":884,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1526],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":41106},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}